What this shows, and what it does not
-------------------------------------
It shows the claim store holds "one funded job, one execution" across processes, which
is what makes SQLite's cross-process write lock the load-bearing part rather than a
single event loop: 50 requests, 1 execution, 1 distinct result, 49 replays, every
response 200 carrying identical bytes, no 5xx.

It is NOT the A2 evaluation. That is SEC-003, which runs the published attack against a
labelled vulnerable fixture *and* against AgentTrust and reports both, with its own run
manifest. The published baseline is 50 replays producing 50 grants with no idempotency
(V-13); putting the two side by side is SEC-003's job, not this file's.
